1
00:00:23,076 --> 00:00:29,076
Panic in the Mailroom is a animation, family,
comedy film directed by Mark O'Hare.

2
00:00:46,153 --> 00:00:52,153
Two Minions are busy at work in the mailroom.

3
00:01:09,230 --> 00:01:15,230
One of them, bored, decides to throw a box of expired
PX-41 samples into its designated chute.

4
00:01:32,307 --> 00:01:38,307
Ken the Minion / Mike the Minion (voice), played by Pierre Coffin.

5
00:01:55,384 --> 00:02:01,384
Gru(voice)(uncredited), played by Steve Carell.

6
00:02:18,461 --> 00:02:24,461
Despicable Me is an American media franchise created by
Sergio Pablos, Cinco Paul and Ken Daurio.

7
00:02:41,538 --> 00:02:47,538
It centers on a supervillain turned secret agent named Gru, his adoptive
daughters, Margo, Edith, and Agnes, and his yellow-colored Minions.

8
00:03:04,615 --> 00:03:10,615
The franchise is produced by Illumination and distributed
by its parent company Universal Pictures.

9
00:03:27,692 --> 00:03:33,692
The franchise began with the 2010 film of the same name, which was followed by three sequels, Despicable Me 2 (2013), Despicable Me
3 (2017), and Despicable Me 4 (2024) and two spin-off prequels, Minions (2015) and Minions: The Rise of Gru (2022).

10
00:03:50,769 --> 00:03:56,769
The franchise also includes many short films, a television special,
several video games, and a theme park attraction.

11
00:04:13,846 --> 00:04:19,846
The film explores themes of madcap comedy, mailroom, short film.

12
00:04:36,923 --> 00:04:42,923
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
